// `src/lib.npk` — THE UMBRELLA. A consumer imports this file and nothing else.
//
// `use` IS NOT TRANSITIVE (`MODULE_REFERENCE.md` §2.3, measured in 0.0.1): a
// symbol imported into a module is not re-exported by it. That is why this
// file exists and why it is a feature — the public surface is a list in ONE
// file that a reviewer reads in one sitting, rather than whatever the module
// graph happens to expose. `meta/specs/API.md` §1 is the list it grows into,
// and `RX-113` records the measurement behind the rules below.
//
// THREE RULES, EACH PAID FOR BY A MEASUREMENT IN 0.0.1. Break any of them and
// the failure appears in the CONSUMER, as `there is no type named X`, with
// nothing wrong at the line that caused it.
//
//   1. EVERY LINE HERE IS `pub use`. A plain `use` re-exports nothing.
//   2. THIS FILE NEVER PLAIN-`use`s A PATH IT ALSO `pub use`s. The first
//      import of a name wins and a later one is silently declined
//      (`symtab_bind_import`, `src/frontend/symbols.npk`), so a plain `use`
//      written above a `pub use` of the same path downgrades the re-export to
//      nothing AT NO DIAGNOSTIC. Provisional workbench question O-N13.
//   3. ONE NAME PER LINE. Several single-name `pub use` lines from one path DO
//      compose — measured, both orders — so the list stays greppable and a
//      removal is one line of diff.
//
// LAYERING. This file is ABOVE `BUILD.md` §6's diagram, not in it: it imports
// `api` (and, as the surface grows, the other layers) and nothing imports it
// except a consumer. `check_layering` (cycle 0.0.3) reads that exception from
// `BUILD.md` §6 rather than special-casing the filename.
mod:lib;

// The public surface, one name per line. TODAY IT IS ONE NAME, and that name
// is the entire cost of importing this library: every consuming program's
// `failsafe` owes exactly one arm, `(ERegexPattern)` (RX-060, `SAFETY.md` S-8).
// `tests/conformance/import.npk` is the program that proves it.
pub use "./api/api.npk".ERegexPattern;
